<title>USA: Peco Energy says cool weather hurt earnings.</title>
<headline>Peco Energy says cool weather hurt earnings.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>PECO Energy Co said on Monday that cooler weather hurt revenues, lowering its earnings by $0.20 per share in the third quarter.</p>
<p>The company today reported third quarter earnings of $0.65 per share, a 19 percent drop from third quarter earnings of $0.80 per share last year.</p>
<p>The company said total electric sales rose 10 percent from the third quarter 1995 mainly from more sales to other utilities, which was partially offset by lower sales from cooler weather conditions.</p>
</text>
